<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">How big are Kawhi Leonard's hands?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Leonard's hands measure 9.75 inches in length and 11.25 inches in width, measured at the 2011 NBA Draft Combine. That width is commonly cited as the third-largest of any active NBA player and remains one of the most distinctive measurements in combine history.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">What is Kawhi Leonard's wingspan?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Leonard's wingspan is 7 feet 3 inches, with a standing reach of 8 feet 10 inches — both measured at the 2011 combine. Combined with his hand size, it's a big part of why he plays defense far longer than his 6-foot-6 barefoot height alone would suggest.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">Why is the Kawhi Leonard trade to the Raptors on hold?</div>
<div class="faq-a">The Clippers and Raptors agreed to the trade on June 30, 2026, but it can't be finalized until the NBA concludes its investigation into whether the Clippers circumvented the salary cap through Leonard's endorsement deal with the now-bankrupt company Aspiration. The Raptors have chosen to wait rather than assume the risk of a penalty affecting Leonard's contract after the trade closes.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">What could happen if the NBA finds wrongdoing?</div>
<div class="faq-a">Leonard's contract could potentially be voided, and the Clippers could face penalties including lost draft picks. The 2000 Joe Smith–Timberwolves case is the closest precedent — Minnesota lost five first-round picks for a similar violation, with two later reinstated on appeal.</div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<div class="faq-q">Was Kawhi Leonard a top combine prospect in 2011?</div>
<div class="faq-a">No — his combine numbers were largely unremarkable for a small forward prospect, which contributed to him sliding to 15th overall. His hand size was the one standout measurement. The Spurs traded for him on draft night based on defensive instincts and shooting touch the combine doesn't test, a bet that led to two Finals MVP awards with two different franchises.</div>
</div>
